Eric Palacios from Eric Palacios and  Associates shares what the traffic laws  are regarding emergency vehicles and  school buses in today's legal minute  hi I'm attorney Eric Palacios welcome to  the legal minute today's question is  what are the traffic laws regarding  emergency vehicles and school buses  first always yield to an emergency  vehicle that has its lights on or sirens  on pull over to your right as soon as  possible don't pull over to the left or  don't simply stop in the middle of the  road if there is a raised median in the  emergency vehicle is coming in the  opposite direction Most states do not  require you to pull over unless there is  a break in the median where the  emergency vehicle can cross over into  your lane next come to a stop if you see  a school bus with the stop signs  activated whether you're going in the  same or opposite direction of the bus  stop until the stop sign is retracted  and there are no more children on the  street this has been the legal minute if  you have any questions you can call our  office at  702-444-7777  that information again for Palacios and  Associates  702-44-777 or you can go to their  website at Eric palacioslaw.com  problem
 

